    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_0d97fca10a341fb23e61b14f32cc203b979382e0c2ae0bc113124f382975ee5a",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Heisenberg time is the resolution threshold linking orbit duration to spectral detail: resolving individual levels requires orbit terms through T_H. At that scale, the Riemann amplitude is exactly negative and exponentially decaying, whereas generic determinant decay is only asymptotic and a fixed negative phase is incompatible with phase multiplication under repeated traversal. Period matching alone therefore cannot validate a candidate dynamics.",
