    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_29c6fe69776ee8c4bc8ae7b5b43eeefd15695e7d18eaf53aa29317dd47ccdd03",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "XP is a compact organizer because one dilation mechanism yields uniform instability, broken time reversal, critical-line power eigenfunctions, and—after an external phase-space cutoff—the smooth zero count, while Fourier duality supplies the zeta theta phase. Testing that package against the coupled Riemann-dynamics constraints localizes the failure at spectral closure: dilation sums can contain zeta without enforcing its zeros, character twists only suggest unconstructed boundary extensions, and position-momentum reinjection gives the near-zero identity with the wrong sign while leaving boundedness, prime primitive periods, and Maslov phases unresolved.",
