    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a52fd8ca940c1306d74f6b387f5bd71114a49212c8f126d6bd0763215f0b99e3",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The diagonal orbit sum and the Hannay-Ozorio rule produce K(tau)=|tau| only below the Heisenberg threshold; discreteness then forces coherent off-diagonal cancellation rather than random-phase disappearance. For Riemann zeros, Hardy-Littlewood prime-pair correlations supply that missing long-time contribution, while retaining short prime orbits and then the unsmoothed singular series separates two finite-height effects: low zeta zeros reappear as resonances in high-zero correlations, and fine arithmetic phases produce the small oscillatory correction to number variance.",
